Source: tapedeck
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ashwin Balaji <s.ashwinbalaji.de@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo-web (>= 1.88) | cargo (>= 1.88),
 rustc-web (>= 1.88) | rustc (>= 1.88), gcc
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://codeberg.org/abksh/tapedeck
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: tapedeck
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: self-hosted scrobbler and listening journal
 Tapedeck records what you listen to from Plex, Jellyfin, Emby, Navidrome,
 Roon and any ListenBrainz-compatible player, enriches it with MusicBrainz
 metadata, keeps it in SQLite, and forwards it to Last.fm, ListenBrainz and
 Libre.fm. It also records how you listened (signal chains and gear), a
 shelf of vinyl, tape and discs, and your own liner notes. The web UI is
 built into the binary.
 .
 The service is installed but not enabled. Set MUSICBRAINZ_CONTACT in
 /etc/tapedeck/tapedeck.env, then: systemctl enable --now tapedeck
